{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel><data id=\"total\" expr=\"0\"/><data id=\"list\" expr=\"[1, 2]\"/></datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <transition event=\"go\" cond=\"total => 1\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"go2\" cond=\"(total) =>  total + 1\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"go3\" cond=\"list.some(x => x &gt; 1)\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"go4\" cond=\"(a, b) => a\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml063-ecmascript-arrow-condition.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":3,"warnings":3},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml063-ecmascript-arrow-condition.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":2,"byteOffset":237,"endColumn":42,"endLine":4,"startColumn":40,"startLine":4},"insertedContent":{"text":">="}}]}],"description":{"text":"compare with `>=`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml063-ecmascript-arrow-condition.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":42,"endLine":4,"startColumn":40,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`cond` on `<transition>` is an arrow function, so it is always true\n\n**Note:** in ECMAScript `x => 1` is a function whose parameter is `x`; a condition is converted to a boolean without calling it, and every function is truthy, so the condition always holds\n\n**Help:** to test whether `total` is at least the value, compare with `>=`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`cond` on `<transition>` is an arrow function, so it is always true"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":239,"start":237},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML063"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml063-ecmascript-arrow-condition.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":2,"byteOffset":298,"endColumn":45,"endLine":5,"startColumn":43,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":">="}}]}],"description":{"text":"compare with `>=`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml063-ecmascript-arrow-condition.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":45,"endLine":5,"startColumn":43,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`cond` on `<transition>` is an arrow function, so it is always true\n\n**Note:** in ECMAScript `x => 1` is a function whose parameter is `x`; a condition is converted to a boolean without calling it, and every function is truthy, so the condition always holds\n\n**Help:** to test whether `total` is at least the value, compare with `>=`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`cond` on `<transition>` is an arrow function, so it is always true"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":300,"start":298},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML063"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml063-ecmascript-arrow-condition.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":44,"endLine":7,"startColumn":42,"startLine":7}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`cond` on `<transition>` is an arrow function, so it is always true\n\n**Note:** in ECMAScript `x => 1` is a function whose parameter is `x`; a condition is converted to a boolean without calling it, and every function is truthy, so the condition always holds\n\n**Help:** a condition must compute a boolean: compare with `>=`, or call the function\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`cond` on `<transition>` is an arrow function, so it is always true"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":442,"start":440},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML063"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`cond=\"count => 3\"` parses as a function whose parameter is `count`; a condition is converted to a boolean without calling it, and every function is truthy, so the transition is always enabled; `>=` was almost always intended"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: compare with `>=` (the finding offers the fix when the parameter is a single name), or call the function to compute a boolean.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML063` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#ConditionalExpressions","id":"SCXML063","name":"SCXML063","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an ECMAScript condition is an arrow function, so it is always true"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}